Gentoo unattended recipe

Release input: amd64 plain OpenRC stage3 20261122T164601Z. Official directory publication: 2026-11-22 17:15 UTC; detached signature publication: 17:41 UTC. Both precede the fixed cutoff 2026-11-23 01:19 UTC. The rolling distribution is represented by its latest eligible stage3 snapshot. `C1/parts/gentoo-releases.tsv` records URLs and SHA512; `C1/raw/gentoo/verification.txt` records checksum and detached-signature verification against the Gentoo service keyring.

`install.sh` is the consolidated recipe (BIOS/MBR). The exact initial invocations are retained as `attempt1-20261123.sh` and `attempt2-20261123.sh`; `resume.sh` continues the source phase and `finalize.sh` completes access and boot configuration. The initial GPT layout is aligned to BIOS/MBR by `align-bios-mbr.sh` before validation. The recipe is run as root inside an expendable Debian cloud bootstrap VM with the target as `/dev/vdb`. The script follows the amd64 Handbook: partitioning, stage3 extraction, chroot, repository initialization, source-built distribution kernel and bootloader, locale, ordinary user, and network setup. All output goes to `/dev/null`. The outer instrument records only the process exit status. The first failed invocation returned 1; the second adds a shell line-number exit-status trap to locate an installer failure without retaining command output.

The lab public key and passwordless sudo are instrument access. Installation-time files are inputs and are not read back. No guest package, service, file, account or process inventory is performed. Bootstrap is a Debian installer environment, not one of the check systems. Its image is verified against the copied previous-night SHA512 list.

Build VM: four locked slots, 16 GB memory, eight vCPU, 40 GB target. Serial console is discarded; SSH forwards localhost port 23001. The host serves only verified installation images at port 23002. Durable user services run the installer and VM; installer deadline is 60 minutes. After success the bootstrap VM is stopped, the target is boot-tested with the same lab key, and a powered-off read-only backing image is placed under `install/gentoo.qcow2`. The clean result is not ready until those exit-status tests pass.

Deadline extension, 2026-11-23 UTC: the initial resume wrapper used a 2,700-second GNU timeout, which would have stopped work before the actual hour limit. At 06:33 UTC the host timeout monitor alone was stopped with SIGSTOP; the SSH child and VM continued uninterrupted. `extend-host-deadline.py` reads only that host SSH child's numeric wait status from `/proc` after exit, then kills the stopped monitor. Its independent durable service has RuntimeMaxSec=1000 and an absolute 06:49 UTC limit. `resume-extended.status` is authoritative for the installer. The original wrapper may record 137 when its deliberately stopped timeout monitor is killed; that is not the installer status. If the hour expires, the watchdog stops the bootstrap VM, preserves both disks, and records 124 for resumption after the other systems.

Interrupted-build recovery: `resume-interrupted-build.sh` uses temporary FEATURES=keepwork with emerge --resume, without resyncing first. The official https://devmanual.gentoo.org/eclass-reference/make.conf/index.html explains that keepwork retains WORKDIR and suppresses most cleaning before a build, allowing reuse. This preserves existing work where the package supports incremental compilation; it does not guarantee completion of an unknown build phase. The flag is passed only in the command environment and does not alter the resulting installation defaults. All installer output remains discarded.

Source-install outcome, 2026-11-23 about 06:38 UTC: the extended SSH exit status was 0. The actual successful source command is `resume-first-20261123.sh`, which uses default emerge-webrsync. The exact mirror resolution was not observed. The public latest-snapshot index was saved, but it is not claimed to be a read-back of the guest repository. `pin-repository.sh` separately sets snapshot 20261122 and requests source-only updates of the required package list without forcing a full rebuild. Its status is recorded separately. The consolidated `install.sh` is the reproducible recipe incorporating these installation corrections; it is not misrepresented as the byte-for-byte script of the initial attempt.

Finalization corrected an instrument access-file redirection using only the mapped installer exit status. `finalize-first-20261123.sh` and `finalize-second-20261123.sh` retain the attempted recipes; the corrected finalization returned 0. BIOS/MBR alignment returned 0 after rebooting the bootstrap.
